# ── Docker build context excludes ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# an image layer. Two things made that actively harmful:
#
#   1. .env holds a real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Copying it into the image ships the
#      secret to the registry, where it survives `docker run -e` overrides and
#      any later key rotation in the hosting dashboard. Secrets belong in the
#      platform's env config, never in a layer.
#   2. venv/ is ~228 MB of Python 3.14 packages. The image is python:3.12-slim
#      and reinstalls from requirements.txt anyway, so this was pure upload —
#      slow builds on a free-tier plan, for bytes that are never read.

# Secrets — provided at runtime by Render/Railway env config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local virtualenvs (image installs from requirements.txt)
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Python bytecode — wrong interpreter version for this base image
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local databases and scratch state
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Docs and deploy manifests — not needed at runtime
BACKEND_SETUP.md
railway.json

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
